hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1377","Yunus bin Abd al-Ala al-Sadfi told us, Ibn Wahb told us, that Malik told him, and al-Rabi’ told us, he said: Al-Shafi’i said, he told us Malik, H. Abu Musa Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna narrated to us, a soul, Malik narrated to us, on the authority of Zaid, who is Ibn Aslam, on the authority of Ata’ bin Yasar On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The sun was eclipsed during the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the people were with him, so he stood for a long time for about Surat Al-Baqarah, then he bowed for a long time, then he rose and stood for a long time, which is less than the first standing, then he bowed for a long time, which is less than the bowing. The first, then he prostrated, then he stood for a long time, which is less than that first standing, then he bowed for a long time, which is less than that first bowing, then he rose So he stood for a long time, which is less than that of the first standing, then he bowed for a long time, which is less than that bowing, then he prostrated, then he left, and he The sun appeared, and he said: “Indeed, the sun and the moon are two of the signs of God. They are not caused by anyone’s death or life, so when you see that, remember God.” They said: O Messenger of God, we saw you eating in this position of yours. Al-Rabi’ said something, then we saw you as if you were bowing down, and the other two said: You were bowing down. He said: “Indeed, I saw Paradise,” and they said: “So I ate a bunch of it, and if I had taken it, you would have eaten from it for the rest of the world.” Al-Rabi’ said: “And I saw or I was shown the fire,” and the other two said: “And I saw the fire,” and they said: “I have never seen a sight like today, and I saw most of its people being women.” Al-Rabi’ said: They said: Why? The other two said: From what, O Messenger of God? He said: “Because of their disbelief.” It was said: Do they disbelieve in God? He said: “They disbelieve in marriage, and they disbelieve in benevolence. If you were good to one of them all the time, and then she saw something from you, she said: I have not seen anything good from you.” “Quit.” Abu Musa said: A soul said: “And the partner is the husband.”"
